# Deny by default: the build needs four things, and everything else is context
# the daemon uploads and never uses (`.venv/` alone is ~1 GB). Listing what is
# allowed rather than what is banned means a new stray file — a dump, a
# notebook, a second `.env` — is excluded until someone opts it in.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!app/
!scripts/

# Build artefacts that live inside the allowed directories.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
